{"name":"Ombre Blue","hex":"#4a4e5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ombre","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Spanish card game, usually played by three people. It involves forty cards, omitting the ranks of 8, 9 and 10."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large Mediterranean food fish, Umbrina cirrosa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ombre"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ombre","blocks":[{"text":"Ombre or omber, also called l'Hombre, is a fast-moving seventeenth-century trick-taking card game for three players. It has been described as \"the most successful card game ever invented.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/The_Four_Friends_Playing_Hombre.JPG/330px-The_Four_Friends_Playing_Hombre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ombre","wikidata":"Q5662149"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Anna_Palm_-_A_game_of_L%27hombre_in_Br%C3%B8ndum%27s_Hotel_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Anna_Palm_-_A_game_of_L%27hombre_in_Br%C3%B8ndum%27s_Hotel_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Anna_Palm_-_A_game_of_L%27hombre_in_Br%C3%B8ndum%27s_Hotel_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Anna_Palm_-_A_game_of_L%27hombre_in_Br%C3%B8ndum%27s_Hotel_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Anna_Palm_-_A_game_of_L%27hombre_in_Br%C3%B8ndum%27s_Hotel_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Anna_Palm_-_A_game_of_L%27hombre_in_Br%C3%B8ndum%27s_Hotel_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Game of L'hombre in Brøndum's Hotel by Swedish artist Anna Palm de Rosa, circa 1885","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnna_Palm_-_A_game_of_L'hombre_in_Br%C3%B8ndum's_Hotel_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Le_Jeu_de_L%27Hombre_1695_edition.jpg/120px-Le_Jeu_de_L%27Hombre_1695_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/98/Le_Jeu_de_L%27Hombre_1695_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Le_Jeu_de_L%27Hombre_1695_edition.jpg/120px-Le_Jeu_de_L%27Hombre_1695_edition.jp